    "content": "Could not connect to a shared browser at http://127.0.0.1:27001.\n\nThe semantic-hints MCP must observe the SAME browser that the Playwright MCP controls, so it connects to a shared Chromium over CDP rather than launching its own.\n\nTo fix:\n  1. Start Chromium with remote debugging, e.g.:\n       chromium --remote-debugging-port=9222\n     (or your local Chrome/Chromium binary).\n  2. Point the Playwright MCP at that same browser if your version supports it.\n  3. Set SEMANTIC_HINTS_CDP_URL (default http://127.0.0.1:9222) to match.\n\nIf you intentionally want an unshared session for standalone testing, set SEMANTIC_HINTS_LAUNCH_BROWSER=true (its state will NOT be shared with Playwright MCP)."
  }
